1
00:00:01,720 --> 00:00:06,160
You think you've got me cornered, but
I've already implemented my tactics.

2
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:08,850
No!

3
00:00:08,933 --> 00:00:09,763
What the!

4
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:28,700
I really hate to say it, but Okuyasu's
brother just about took me out for good.

5
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:32,871
Koichi, I think it's high time
we got the hell out of here.

6
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:33,870
Huh?

7
00:00:33,953 --> 00:00:35,753
But what about the bow and arrow he had?

8
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:36,821
Where did it go?

9
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:37,960
Good memory.

10
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:41,617
Bastard must have hit it somewhere
after he dragged you up the stairs.

11
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:43,157
Don't tell me you wanna...

12
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:44,070
Yeah.

13
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,288
Hold off on looking for it.

14
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:49,737
If their dad bought this
place, he may still be around.

15
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:52,717
Plus, I'm too badly hurt
to be of much help to you.

16
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,337
Let's just leave it be for now.

17
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:55,250
No!

18
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:56,331
We can't just do nothing!

19
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:57,930
Look,

20
00:00:58,013 --> 00:01:01,297
the only reason I'm alive right now is
because you healed my wounds with your stand.

21
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:02,397
But think about it.

22
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:04,917
If somebody else gets shot
with that bow and arrow,

23
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,397
Let's face it, they're probably gonna die!

24
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:08,774
Is that what you want?

25
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:12,197
You can stay here and rest up.

26
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,637
Don't worry about me.

27
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:15,240
I'll find it by myself.

28
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:17,957
And truth be told.

29
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:21,569
I'm not so sure their dad even
lives in this house anymore?.

30
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:24,417
I mean, if he was living here?

31
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:26,676
He would have come out by now, right?

32
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:33,231
He may not look it, but Koichi
has a hell of a lot of guts.

33
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:37,037
At least when things get
tough, or he's not in his head.

34
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:39,817
But that won't mean a thing if
we don't make it out of here.

35
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:41,980
We need to leave as fast as we can.

36
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:47,530
Hey!

37
00:01:47,613 --> 00:01:48,443
Oh, it's you!

38
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,477
What, you trying to stop me?

39
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:51,390
Not a chance.

40
00:01:51,980 --> 00:01:56,117
We're gonna snap that bow and arrow in
two, then say goodbye to this hellhole.

41
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:57,030
Together.

42
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:31,860
There's an attic.

43
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,176
The bow and arrow's probably up here.

44
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:45,580
There it is!

45
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:46,859
The bow and arrow!

46
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:48,980
And it's just hanging on the wall!

47
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:58,180
That doesn't sound good.

48
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:00,748
Something must be in there.

49
00:04:04,140 --> 00:04:06,797
Well, at least it's
chained up, whatever it is.

50
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:08,457
You think it could be a dog?

51
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:10,716
Because it's definitely not a person.

52
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:14,520
Well, if it is, it sure isn't happy.

53
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:28,817
What are we supposed to do?

54
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:29,997
I'm too scared to think.

55
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:32,837
By asking me, I voted to
leave this house of horrors.

56
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:34,377
I know, but...

57
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:36,220
We can't just turn back now.

58
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:37,677
All right, Koichi,

59
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:41,297
on the count of three, I want you to bust
the door open with everything you've got.

60
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:42,437
That should scare it.

61
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:46,377
Then I'll run over as fast as I can
and break that bow and arrow in half.

62
00:04:46,460 --> 00:04:47,290
You got it?

63
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:49,090
Yeah.

64
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:53,120
Let's go.

65
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:58,500
One, two, three!

66
00:05:02,420 --> 00:05:03,340
What the hell?!

67
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:05,130
Koichi!

68
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:09,300
Help me! Wait a minute.

69
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:10,697
That thing is no stand.

70
00:05:10,780 --> 00:05:13,517
It's a real hand attached
to a real funky-looking arm!

71
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:14,541
Help me, please!

72
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:17,210
Char!

73
00:05:21,340 --> 00:05:22,170
Fuck!

74
00:05:22,253 --> 00:05:23,960
I wasn't trying to sever it.

75
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:01,140
Hey, Koichi, what the hell is that thing?

76
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:05,077
I can't believe something like that
was living right under our noses.

77
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:06,240
Uh, gross.

78
00:06:06,980 --> 00:06:08,220
So you found him.

79
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:10,660
That was never supposed to happen.

80
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:14,940
You again.

81
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:21,200
It's a long story, but he's our father.

82
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:27,240
If you can believe it and right
now he needs these more than you.

83
00:06:29,300 --> 00:06:31,097
Why is he grabbing the bow and arrow?

84
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:35,897
It's imperative that I find
more stand users for my father.

85
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:38,297
So no one is getting these.

86
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:40,057
Come at me with all your might.

87
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:42,717
If you must, I'll protect
him until the bitter end.

88
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:46,357
So did a disease do this
to your dad? A disease.

89
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:47,357
You're joking.

90
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:50,297
Dad is an excellent
health minus the warts.

91
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:52,357
He even has a hearty appetite.

92
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:55,057
And all he does is moan.

93
00:06:55,140 --> 00:06:58,117
It's safe to say he has
no idea I'm his son.

94
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:00,697
So you've been searching for a stand user

95
00:07:00,780 --> 00:07:03,700
with the power to cure
your father to cure him.

96
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,557
What are you offering?

97
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:08,240
Because you're not needed.

98
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:15,830
You're wrong.

99
00:07:15,913 --> 00:07:19,517
I've been searching for a stand
user who can kill my father.

100
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:22,247
But at this point, I
doubt it'll ever happen.

101
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:25,140
No matter what I do, Dad won't die.

102
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:29,780
I could bash his head in or chop
his body into a million tiny pieces.

103
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:32,749
Even slicing him to
ribbons won't kill him.

104
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:38,100
I just want to end his suffering.

105
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:42,441
As a kid, I swore to do everything
in my power to make that happen.

106
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:46,557
But I need the bow and arrow in order
to make good on my promise to him.

107
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:51,560
If I hand these over to you, dad
will be a freak for all eternity.

108
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:53,330
Suffering.

109
00:07:53,413 --> 00:07:56,077
All because some bastard
named Dio decided to

110
00:07:56,160 --> 00:08:00,140
implant cells in his skull and
make my dad a monster! Hold on.

111
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:01,900
Did you say Dio?

112
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:03,060
The guy from Mr.

113
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,162
Jotaro's story.

114
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:09,720
Indulge me by listening
to how things used to be.

115
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:12,040
Josuke Higashikata.

116
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:17,200
Although what I'm about to tell you
is related to your life as well.

117
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:20,820
Everything began 11 years ago.

118
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:23,700
1988 was the beginning of the end.

119
00:08:24,620 --> 00:08:28,160
I was 7 that year and my
brother Okuyasu was just 4.

120
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:31,557
We were living in Tokyo during this time.

121
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:34,997
It was the middle of the bubble
economy and spirits were high.

122
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:38,920
Well, the spirits of
everyone except my father.

123
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:41,460
Mom fell sick and died.

124
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:46,536
When Dad's business went under, he
was buried under a mountain of debt.

125
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:52,720
He'd often beat us for no reason.

126
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:55,640
It was the walking definition of a loser.

127
00:08:58,200 --> 00:09:00,220
That's when everything changed.

128
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:05,560
Out of the blue, a seemingly endless
supply of cash started rolling in.

129
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:09,392
And on top of that, there were
jewels and precious metals.

130
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:12,100
But Dad didn't have a job to speak of.

131
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:16,669
After some research,
I found out the truth.

132
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:18,604
My father had made a dark deal.

133
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:21,880
He sold his own soul to
a man by the name of Dio.

134
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:25,080
He became Dio's lackey for monetary gain.

135
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,880
Based on what I found out,

136
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:32,957
Dio's goal was to scour the globe
in search of potential stand users.

137
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:37,320
And somehow, he discovered my dad
had the capacity to manifest a stand.

138
00:09:37,860 --> 00:09:42,400
However, to this day, I have no idea
what the nature of his stand is.

139
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:44,680
And then things changed again.

140
00:09:45,340 --> 00:09:48,516
It's been ten years, but I
remember it like yesterday.

141
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:51,987
It was two in the afternoon.

142
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:55,167
I'd just come home from
a long day at school.

143
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:57,710
Okuyasu!

144
00:09:58,020 --> 00:09:59,844
Did that bastard hit you again?

145
00:09:59,940 --> 00:10:01,234
What's wrong with him?

146
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:03,700
No, he didn't.

147
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:12,090
Dio!

148
00:10:12,173 --> 00:10:13,003
Dio is dead!

149
00:10:13,086 --> 00:10:14,960
That must be the reason!

150
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:17,930
Dad?

151
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,310
Dad?

152
00:10:22,460 --> 00:10:23,813
I'll call an ambulance!

153
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:25,320
It's no use!

154
00:10:25,460 --> 00:10:26,320
I'm not sick!

155
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:28,678
The flesh blood is ravaging my body!

156
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,420
This is the end! Dad!

157
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:35,672
After a year, he didn't know who we were.

158
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:38,277
The man had forgotten all
about his own children

159
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:40,772
and had become a muttering glob of flesh.

160
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:47,297
Dio used to implant his own cells
into the minds of those he distrusted

161
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:51,100
so he could manipulate his victims
in whatever way he saw fit.

162
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:55,625
And as you can guess, he implanted
one of those things into Dad.

163
00:10:58,380 --> 00:11:01,177
For 10 years i threw myself into research

164
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:05,717
i studied stands i learned about jotaro In

165
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:08,557
my studies i learned of anyaba the hag and

166
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:11,237
obtained possession of
the bow and arrow But

167
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:14,017
in the process i slowly resigned myself to

168
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:16,197
the fact that dad would never recover from

169
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:19,357
The curse that plagued him my father had

170
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:22,322
already become one with
the immortal cells of dio

171
00:11:22,980 --> 00:11:25,417
Now he spends his days
doing nothing but this.

172
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:27,120
It's infuriating to watch.

173
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:30,957
Every moment of every day
for the past ten years,

174
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:33,922
he's scratched around that
stupid box of rubbish.

175
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:37,840
If I confiscate it, he wails
and groans for days on end.

176
00:11:38,140 --> 00:11:39,787
I'm sick of dealing with it.

177
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:41,520
Look at his putrid face.

178
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:44,838
Makes me disgusted with the
very idea of life itself.

179
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:50,240
I've told you over and
over, stop making a mess!

180
00:11:53,900 --> 00:11:58,240
Though I've noticed, when I discipline
the bastard, he seems to hear me!

181
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:01,480
And he keeps rummaging in his own filth!

182
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:03,720
But I guess the swine can't help it!

183
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:07,030
Enough!

184
00:12:07,113 --> 00:12:08,417
You're the one who needs to stop!

185
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:10,441
He's still your father, isn't he?

186
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,118
Yeah, you're right.

187
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:16,980
This man is my father, but in blood only.

188
00:12:17,580 --> 00:12:21,639
The detestable thing I see before
me isn't the father I used to know.

189
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:26,100
This man sold his soul to Dio and
is living the life he created.

190
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:28,998
But I'm not totally without a heart.

191
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:32,796
Seeing my one and only father
like this is unbearable.

192
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:34,607
You don't know how it feels.

193
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:39,440
All I want to do is end his life and
finally free him from this suffering.

194
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:45,154
And by putting him out of his misery,
I'll be able to live my life again.

195
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:54,140
What did I say?

196
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:56,497
I've had just about enough of you!

197
00:12:56,580 --> 00:12:58,286
Get out of the box right now!

198
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:00,390
Hey!

199
00:13:00,473 --> 00:13:02,021
You've more than made your point!

200
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:05,397
Sorry, but I just can't let
you have this bow and arrow!

201
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,740
Not now or ever!

202
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,220
That works for me!

203
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:10,873
I'll just take that bow and arrow later!

204
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:15,200
But right now, my sights
are set on that box!

205
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:18,080
Wait, the box?

206
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:32,877
It was clear from the way he
was clutching those scraps

207
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:36,195
of paper that there was
something important about them.

208
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:38,060
Now it makes sense.

209
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:48,480
A family photo.

210
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:51,489
He knew what he was doing.

211
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:54,897
He hasn't been mindlessly rummaging
through that box for ten years.

212
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:55,997
He's had a purpose.

213
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:59,727
He was looking for the photo of
his sons when they were young.

214
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:04,057
It's true that he's not completely
aware of his surroundings.

215
00:14:04,140 --> 00:14:06,840
But deep down, his
memories are still intact.

216
00:14:07,700 --> 00:14:09,160
Memories of better days.

217
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:44,371
Give up on looking for a stand that kills,

218
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:47,938
because if you focus on
using one that heals instead,

219
00:14:49,060 --> 00:14:50,766
Then I'm willing to help you.

220
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:58,847
But first you'll have to hand over that
bow and arrow, because they're history.

221
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:04,658
You're not planning to run, are you?

222
00:15:07,060 --> 00:15:08,220
Bro, please.

223
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:09,920
Enough is enough.

224
00:15:12,140 --> 00:15:13,320
Okuyasu, come on.

225
00:15:13,540 --> 00:15:14,893
Let's end this already.

226
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:17,473
There's no point in fighting him, right?

227
00:15:17,840 --> 00:15:19,075
So, you stuck around.

228
00:15:20,340 --> 00:15:21,460
What do you say?

229
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:24,699
There's a chance that could
get better, couldn't he?

230
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:29,006
So what if he doesn't
look the way he used to?

231
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:31,541
That stuff doesn't really matter.

232
00:15:31,760 --> 00:15:35,054
The important thing is, he'd
have his memories and soul.

233
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:36,030
Right?

234
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,647
Nokuyasu, the hell do
you think you're doing?

235
00:15:45,020 --> 00:15:45,850
Bro.

236
00:15:47,260 --> 00:15:48,740
Move it, Okuyasu!

237
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:52,917
Don't you see it's far too late for me
to just turn my back on the mission?

238
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,197
I've already slaughtered
countless people in this

239
00:15:55,280 --> 00:15:58,162
town with the very bow
and arrow you're gripping!

240
00:15:58,300 --> 00:16:01,947
Besides, as far as I'm concerned,
you're no longer my brother.

241
00:16:02,180 --> 00:16:05,860
As such, I have no qualms about
killing you where you stand.

242
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:09,990
Bro...

243
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:18,730
Question.

244
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:22,547
Is there anyone else living here
besides you two and your dad?

245
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:23,630
Others?

246
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:25,700
No, it's just the three of us.

247
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:35,890
That's...

248
00:16:35,973 --> 00:16:37,227
it's coming from the outlet.

249
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:41,920
Okuyasu, pull your head
out of your ass, you idiot!

250
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:45,660
No! It broke!

251
00:16:47,260 --> 00:16:51,060
I'll be relieving you of this
bow and arrow, Keicho Nijimura!

252
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:53,457
You do still remember me, don't you?

253
00:16:53,540 --> 00:16:57,128
Since you awakened my stand when
you shot me with this arrow!

254
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:59,960
I do, and you are an idiot!

255
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:02,197
You can't handle the bow and arrow!

256
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:03,580
Keicho Nijimura!

257
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:06,134
Stands are a manifestation of the soul!

258
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:08,277
I've matured since you told me that!

259
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:12,560
But let me guess, you weren't
expecting my stand, Chili Pepper,

260
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:14,317
to evolve to this degree!

261
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:16,580
War's company, attack!

262
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:17,780
No more words!

263
00:17:18,380 --> 00:17:20,380
Hey, is that electricity?

264
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:23,337
Okuyasu's brother is turning into it!

265
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:25,067
And so is the bow and arrow!

266
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:26,410
No!

267
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:28,220
No! Get back!

268
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,180
Don't touch me!

269
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:32,100
You'll get sucked into!

270
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:34,490
Big bro...

271
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:36,540
This isn't good!

272
00:17:36,820 --> 00:17:37,880
All that work!

273
00:17:38,260 --> 00:17:40,378
And he's stealing the bow and arrow!

274
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:44,560
Okuyasu, I knew you'd find
a way to screw me over.

275
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:48,240
Ever since we were kids,
you've always held me back.

276
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:51,700
It broke!

277
00:17:56,980 --> 00:17:57,810
Josuke!

278
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:08,147
There's no doubt in my mind that a stand
user was watching us from that window.

279
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:12,062
Did you recognize that
stand back there, Okuyasu?

280
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:13,877
I didn't.

281
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:16,057
Bro was the one who found the STAND users,

282
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:19,199
and when he did, he didn't
tell me a lot about them.

283
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:28,380
Josuke, look! It's...

284
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:38,150
Okuyasu.

285
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:43,907
Bro, I knew it was only a matter
of time before this happened.

286
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:48,472
I knew all the bad things he did in
his life would catch up to him one day.

287
00:18:49,560 --> 00:18:52,240
But still, in the end, my brother!

288
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:57,340
My brother used his dying moments
to save my life, didn't he?

289
00:18:58,140 --> 00:19:00,240
Josuke, you saw it, right?

290
00:19:01,360 --> 00:19:03,740
Yeah, I couldn't have said it better.

291
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:08,184
Whatever is false, your
brother saved your life.

292
00:19:29,100 --> 00:19:33,060
Would this happen to be Jotaro Kujo?

293
00:19:34,460 --> 00:19:36,166
I don't recognize your voice.

294
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:38,297
Who is this and what do you want from me?

295
00:19:38,380 --> 00:19:40,880
The who doesn't matter, Jotaro Kujo.

296
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:45,551
But as for what I want, I'm kindly
asking you to get the hell out of Morioh.

297
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:48,177
Now let me see if I've got this straight.

298
00:19:48,260 --> 00:19:51,577
A complete stranger calls and
wants me to just up and leave town.

299
00:19:51,660 --> 00:19:54,484
What would you do if the
situation was reversed?

300
00:19:54,620 --> 00:19:57,326
Doesn't matter since I
have the bow and arrow.

301
00:19:58,360 --> 00:19:59,190
That's right.

302
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:02,357
I took it from Keicho
Nijimura after I killed him.

303
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:04,969
and I don't mind getting
rid of you either.

304
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:07,041
I've heard all about you, Jotaro,

305
00:20:07,260 --> 00:20:10,907
that you have the ability to
stop time for one or two seconds.

306
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:13,077
But since you're such a tough guy,

307
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:16,257
I thought I'd take a shot at
convincing you over the phone first.

308
00:20:16,340 --> 00:20:17,840
Are you a stand user too?

309
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:20,377
What do you want with the bow and arrow?

310
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:23,837
I don't mean to cause you any trouble,
if that's what you're implying.

311
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:27,273
And as long as Josuke Higashikata
minds his own business,

312
00:20:27,520 --> 00:20:29,417
I won't lay a finger on him either.

313
00:20:29,500 --> 00:20:32,380
I haven't had this stand
ability for too long,

314
00:20:32,580 --> 00:20:36,397
so my only priority right now
is to have a little fun I've had

315
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:40,598
enough of dealing with mundane things
like entrance exams and resumes.

316
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,500
So you're a student, huh?

317
00:20:43,120 --> 00:20:45,420
What difference does that make? Listen,

318
00:20:45,660 --> 00:20:47,117
if you wear out your welcome,

319
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:49,697
I'll kill you and Josuke
in ways that'll haunt you

320
00:20:49,780 --> 00:20:52,721
How many other stand users
are there in this town?

321
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:00,980
Ha ha ha ha ha!

322
00:21:07,820 --> 00:21:09,480
Here we go again.

323
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:17,480
Keicho Nijimura was buried in Kunimi
Peak Cemetery, west of Morioh.

324
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:21,320
However, the bow and
arrow remains missing.

325
00:21:22,120 --> 00:21:27,580
For Okuyasu Nijimura, it was time to step
up and look after his father for a while.

326
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:29,070
end.

327
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:35,300
Josuke, can you get that?

328
00:21:37,680 --> 00:21:38,640
Good morning.

329
00:21:40,520 --> 00:21:41,480
Hey, Josuke!

330
00:21:41,820 --> 00:21:43,467
Time to go to school, buddy!

331
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:44,950
Huh?

332
00:21:45,033 --> 00:21:48,537
Starting today, the two of us are
going to be going to the same school.

333
00:21:48,620 --> 00:21:51,037
Even so, that doesn't mean
you have to come and get me.

334
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:52,826
This isn't elementary school.

335
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:54,150
No way!

336
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:58,017
You know, I never realized your house
and my house were so close together.

337
00:21:58,100 --> 00:21:58,930
Yeah, shocking.

338
00:21:59,013 --> 00:22:00,857
But like I said, you don't
need to walk me to school.

339
00:22:00,940 --> 00:22:01,770
Come on!

340
00:22:01,853 --> 00:22:03,097
You don't want us to be late!

341
00:22:03,180 --> 00:22:04,010
Hey there!

342
00:22:04,093 --> 00:22:05,597
Are you one of Josuke's friends?

343
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:06,510
Hi!

344
00:22:06,593 --> 00:22:07,820
I'm Okuyasu Nijimura!

345
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:11,297
Come on in and have some coffee
while he finishes getting ready.

346
00:22:11,380 --> 00:22:12,210
Wow, really?

347
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:13,740
Don't mind if I do!

348
00:22:15,620 --> 00:22:17,757
Have you noticed that
your mom's kinda hot?

349
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:19,140
I'm right behind ya!

350
00:22:20,060 --> 00:22:21,017
A comedian.

351
00:22:21,100 --> 00:22:21,930
Just great.

352
00:22:22,013 --> 00:22:23,120
What have I done?

353
00:23:25,920 --> 00:23:31,160
Oh, I want you, I don't
know if I need you, but ooh,

354
00:23:31,620 --> 00:23:33,480
I'm trying to find you.
